<section class="hp-sec reveal not-content" aria-label="What Shadow is">
	<div class="hp-wrap">
		<p class="hp-intro">
			<strong>Shadow is an open-source privacy layer that sits between your apps and AI providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic and Google Gemini.</strong>{' '}
			It finds personal data, customer names, credentials and internal identifiers in every outbound prompt, replaces them with
			realistic, format-preserving fakes, and translates the fakes back in the response. It is PII redaction and AI data loss
			prevention that keeps ChatGPT-style assistants, Claude, coding agents and your own LLM apps useful. It runs as a local
			HTTPS proxy, a gateway base URL, a Docker sidecar or the <code>shadow-core</code> Rust library, and the mapping between
			real and fake values never leaves the machine.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>
